language_server_rust {
    A Rust binary replaces the Langium language-server process.
    The extension launches `reqlan-lsp` over stdio.
    Open `.rq` buffers parse with [parser_rust].
    The open sequence is ["open-file-sequencing.rq".open_file_algorithm].
    Workspace names and rename targets come from the ideas index under [application_memory].
    Inbound hints wait for the host snapshot of that index.
    The inbound inlay hover is markdown. It lists each referencer as a file link.
    An idea hover shows styled idea content when ["../syntax/features-syntax.rq".idea_content_tooltip] is on.
    A closed file has no retained syntax tree.
    Go-to-definition cost is ["../syntax/features-syntax-highlighting.rq".reference_goto_definition_speed].
    When the engine is `rust`, the server also serves `rq:[…]` links and missing-idea diagnostics in non-`.rq` comments.
    One resolution supplies the link and the underline.
    The host serves those links when the engine is `node`.
    Host commands prefer LSP custom requests, napi extract, and the ideas index.
    Move/delete planners still use Langium until index-backed planners land.
    The setting `reqlan.languageServer.engine` selects the binary.
    The default is `rust`.
    `node` remains only when the setting says so, or when the binary is not on disk yet.
    A local extension build compiles this binary with the napi addon ([extension_host_native_stage]).
    The extension launches `bin/reqlan-lsp`, else that release build. It never launches a debug build, because a debug build is slow and the extension build does not refresh it.
    Code actions match ["../vsc-primitives.rq".code_actions]: ignore, create below, import fixes, search or wrap, idea move and delete, and barrel page.
    Attribute and name catalogs drive completion. Rename and find-references use open buffers plus the ideas index.
    Inlay hints honour `reqlan.referencesInlayHints.enabled` and the host inbound snapshot.
    An import link uses the parser token span ([import_from]).
    The path links to the file.
    An imported idea name and its alias each link to that declaration.
    A namespace reference links the alias and the idea as separate names.
    A missing leaf reports an unresolved idea on that name.
    Related: [language_server], [grammar_and_parser], [analytical_rust_port], [vsix_export].
    @status in-progress
    @todo Move/delete and barrel-page host planners still call Langium DI. Finish those off napi/index/LSP.
